1 _OID 0779298c-1bc0-4ad3-9df1-67a07405fbb9
1 _META <metadataxml><content><line>&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;</line><line>&lt;p align="LEFT"&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: medium;"&gt;OBITUARY OF EMELY H. SIEGEL&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</line><line>&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;span style="font-size: medium;"
2 CONC &gt;Death Claims Mrs. J. F. Siegel&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</line><line>&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;span style="font-size: medium;"&gt;Mrs. J. F. Siegel, whose serious illness has been noted frequently in The Times during the past few weeks, passed away a
2 CONC t midnight, Saturday night at Sioux Valley Hospital, after a brave struggle to recover from an &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: medium;"&gt;illness that had lasted over a number of months.&amp;nbsp; Mrs. Siegel, whose maiden name was Emely H
2 CONC . Callaghan, was born Oct. 15, 1854 in Benton county Iowa*. There she grew to womanhood and was married to James L. Hill on Jan. 25, 1871. Shortly after their marriage they moved to Illinois and sixteen years later they came to Cherokee county, Iow
2 CONC a. To this union nine children were born. Two boys preceded the mother into the great beyond. The living are: Ellen J. Like, Slayton, Minn.; Melissa W. Smith, Burlington, Kan.; Ida Cowell, Albany, Oregon, Gertie L. of Albany, Oregon, Henry L. and C
2 CONC layton L. of Cherokee.&amp;nbsp; Her husband died in Cherokee county March 6, 1887.&amp;nbsp; Nov. 9, 1892 she was married to J. F. Siegel. To this union two children were born: Fred J. Siegel of this city and Mrs. Esther E. Becker of Aurelia.&amp;
2 CONC nbsp; She is survived by her husband, 9 children, 36 and grand children and 14 great grandchildren.&amp;nbsp; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: medium;"&gt;Two years ago last November she submitted to an operation in hopes of restoring her fa
2 CONC iling health, but it did not bring about the desired results. So on December 16 she submitted to a second operation. This also failed to prolong her life, and on Saturday at midnight, January 8, at the Sioux Valley hospital, she passed over the gre
2 CONC at divide.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</line><line>&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;span style="font-size: medium;"&gt;Mrs. Siegel united with the Church of Christ over six years ago and remained a consistant follower of her Master to the end. She was a good comp
2 CONC anion, a kind mother, a splendid homemaker. She had a kindly smile &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: medium;"&gt;and a cheerful word for every one who came in to her presence.&amp;nbsp; Funeral services will be held at the Church of Christ a
2 CONC t 1:00 o'clock this afternoon and will be conducted by her pastor, Rev. William Baier. Internment will be made in the Afton cemetery.&amp;nbsp; The entire community extends its deepest sympathy to the bereaved family and relatives in this sadest o
2 CONC f afflictions&lt;span style="font-family: times new roman;"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</line><line>&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: medium;"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: times new roman;"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;span styl
2 CONC e="font-size: medium;"&gt;[*1870, 1880, 1900, 1910, 1920 Federal&amp;nbsp;census and 1915 State census&amp;nbsp;indicates that Emily Callahan&amp;nbsp;was born in Illinois.&amp;nbsp; A 1856 Census from LeRoy twp, Benton Co, Iowa list Emily as 2 an
2 CONC d born in Illinois.]&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</line></content></metadataxml>
